      "date": "2026-04-15T11:35:04.000Z",
      "title": "Dividend increased to ₹110",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹110 is 5.3% higher than last year. Ex-date: 3rd July 2026 Payment date: 19th August 2026 Dividend yield will be 2.7%, which is higher than the industry average of 0.6%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by earnings (76% earnings payout ratio) but not covered by cash flows (272% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 12% per year over the past 10 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. EPS is expected to grow by 11% over the next 2 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "49f8ec15-db94-4d20-b94d-fe1f0a1a0a4b",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-14T18:27:02.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹162 (vs ₹137 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹162 (up from ₹137 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹20.2b (up 20% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹1.96b (up 18% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 9.7% (in line with FY 2025). Revenue is forecast to grow 4.6% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 13% growth forecast for the Machinery industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 14% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 36% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
